   default: 0.186
   description: "Half-width [m] of the car-width strip the scene-mask stats count WALL points in. MUST equal vehicle_frames.front_side_limit_m() (swept_clearance_body_half_width_m 0.136 + front_beside_body_margin_m 0.05): one strip for the whole pipeline, so 'the camera sees a wall in the way' and 'the LiDAR sees a wall in the way' mean the same geometry. Overridable only to test; the node's default IS the shared helper."
 front_clearance_scene_mask_self_polygons:
-  default: ""
-  description: "SELF-mask polygons as JSON [[[x, y], ...], ...] in FRACTIONS of image width/height (a ROS parameter cannot hold a ragged nested list). EMPTY, the default, derives the one polygon from lidar_exclusion_x_min/_x_max/_y_min/_y_max, the car's-own-LiDAR-housing rectangle yolo_detector_node already applies to detections: one calibration, now three consumers, and no second copy of the numbers to drift. Set this only to override that rectangle with a real polygon once one has been traced on a frame."
+  default: '[[[0.8172, 0.7833], [0.8125, 0.8028], [0.8156, 0.9], [0.8359, 0.95], [0.8703, 0.9972], [0.9984, 0.9972], [0.9984, 0.7611], [0.8812, 0.7444], [0.8359, 0.7583]]]'
+  description: "SELF-mask polygons as JSON [[[x, y], ...], ...] in FRACTIONS of image width/height (a ROS parameter cannot hold a ragged nested list). TRACED from corridor10m_20261015T171753 (output/self_mask_proposal/): the LiDAR housing is an orange cap in the bottom-right corner and this is its own contour across all 28 clean RGB frames, plus an 8 px margin at 640x360. It REPLACES the rectangle derived from lidar_exclusion_x_min/_x_max/_y_min/_y_max, which covered 11.25% of the frame to mask 3.61% of hardware: three quarters of that rectangle was live floor, the foot of a fire extinguisher and a glass wall at a median 1.5 m. The traced polygon covers 100% of the hardware in 4.30% of the frame and masks nothing new, freeing 6.95 points of the frame once the occluded-lens polygon is counted. NOT traced from depth: on this rig no pixel is ever persistently -Inf and no depth is ever under 0.3 m, while 9.96% of the frame is persistently unmatched GLASS and textureless floor -- depth cannot tell the car from a window here. EMPTY falls back to the derived rectangle. The same four fractions are still used, unshrunk, by the ROI path and by yolo_detector_node: this parameter changes the scene mask only."
 front_clearance_scene_mask_occluded_polygons:
